diff --git a/docs/contracts/pass-and-output-contracts.md b/docs/contracts/pass-and-output-contracts.md
index 0e1900461..bf8113505 100644
--- a/docs/contracts/pass-and-output-contracts.md
+++ b/docs/contracts/pass-and-output-contracts.md
@@ -60,3 +60,28 @@ Risk if broken:
 - Prefer additive-safe formatting changes and keep legacy column ordering where possible.
 - Treat parser-facing output layout as a contract, not a cosmetic detail.
 - If a contract change is unavoidable, release notes must call out expected downstream updates.
+
+## Opt-in water transfer observations
+
+With `wepp_observe.on` present and `wepp_observe_frost.on` absent, `WCL_*`
+records in `wepp_observe.log` expose stored values without modifying simulation
+state. `WCL_RAW_Q` is terminal runoff depth (m) and volume (m3);
+`WCL_RAW_L` is lateral and tile depth (m); `WCL_AREA` is terminal length and
+width (m); `WCL_GW` is baseflow and deep seepage volume (m3).
+The record's element field identifies the standalone hillslope, channel field
+identifies its terminal OFE, and year/day identify the simulated day. Standalone
+hill IDs must be joined through the run card and PASS filename.
+
+`WCL_SELECTED` exposes lateral/tile arguments before serialization, with event
+enum in the segment field (0=no event, 1=subevent, 2=event). These arguments
+are not necessarily retained in the payload: event selection may omit them.
+`WCL_READ_Q/L/T/G` expose the actual reader arrays before routing; Q/L/T are
+depth (m) and volume (m3), G is baseflow/seepage volume (m3), and element is the
+reader hill index. L excludes the separately observed tile contribution.
+
+Only WCL records use expanded numeric precision; existing observation tags and
+scientific output schemas are unchanged. Retain the actual HBP identity and join
+its calendar/event metadata before interpreting these diagnostics. A small
+channel balance residual does not prove correct transfer dates or complete
+domain closure. Observation I/O can add substantial overhead, particularly on
+network filesystems; use isolated retained replay directories.
diff --git a/src/wepp_observe.for b/src/wepp_observe.for
index 6a693e3e5..45c929680 100644
--- a/src/wepp_observe.for
+++ b/src/wepp_observe.for
@@ -41,10 +41,16 @@ c     in hot paths when observability is disabled (the common production case).
 
       open(unit=lun,file='wepp_observe.log',status='unknown',
      1  position='append',form='formatted')
-      write (lun,1000) tag, year, sdate, ielmt, ichan, iseg, v1, v2
+      if (index(tag,'WCL').eq.1) then
+        write (lun,1010) tag, year, sdate, ielmt, ichan, iseg, v1, v2
+      else
+        write (lun,1000) tag, year, sdate, ielmt, ichan, iseg, v1, v2
+      endif
       close(lun)
 
       return
  1000 format (a,' y=',i6,' d=',i4,' e=',i4,' c=',i4,' s=',i4,
      1  ' v1=',1pe12.4,' v2=',1pe12.4)
+ 1010 format (a,' y=',i6,' d=',i4,' e=',i6,' c=',i4,' s=',i4,
+     1  ' v1=',1pe24.16,' v2=',1pe24.16)
       end
